{"findings":[{"rule_id":"WPS-004","evidence":[{"kind":"dimension","ref":"D12","page":1,"quote":"⌀ 16 H7 (+0.018/0)"},{"kind":"title_block","ref":"surface_treatment","page":1,"quote":"I.Z.B.P. (TRIVALENT)"}],"comment":"The ⌀16 H7 bore carries a tight ISO fit tolerance of 0.018 mm, but the drawing does not account for the added thickness of the I.Z.B.P. plating; after plating the hole will be undersize and the intended fit will fail. The designer should either reduce the pre-plate bore size to allow for the coating thickness or add a note requiring re-machining/re-boring after plating."
  ,
  "recommended_correction":"Reduce the pre-plate bore size by twice the maximum plating thickness, or specify that the ⌀16 H7 bore is to be machined to final size after plating."}]}
